# tests/ is deliberately excluded from the sdist, not partially included.
# An independent reviewer found the default sdist shipped every test .py
# file but none of tests/fixtures/'s non-.py support files (YAML, JSON,
# shell scripts, a symlink) -- 26 of 104 tests then failed for anyone
# installing from the sdist, with failures that read as defects in the
# code rather than a packaging gap. Nothing in this project's actual
# workflow (CI, `uv sync --extra dev`, README's own instructions) tests
# from a downloaded sdist -- only from a git checkout -- so there's
# nothing to preserve by including tests/ at all, and "ship it correctly
# or not at all" is a smaller surface to get wrong than "ship it and
# enumerate every fixture file type as we add them."
prune tests
